<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xmlns:rng="http://relaxng.org/ns/structure/1.0" xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron" xml:lang="en">
  <teiHeader>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>The Solemne TEI schema</title>
        <author>Gleb Schmidt</author>
        <author>Friederike Voit</author>
        <author>Sven Meeder</author>
      </titleStmt>
      <editionStmt>
        <edition n="0.1.0">Version 0.1.0</edition>
      </editionStmt>
      <publicationStmt>
        <publisher>SOLEMNE: The Social Life of Early Medieval Normative Texts, Radboud University</publisher>
        <availability>
          <licence target="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">This ODD, the guide: CC BY 4.0.</licence>
          <licence target="https://opensource.org/license/mit">The schema generated from it: MIT. It contains
            material of TEI P5 (the TEI Consortium: CC BY 3.0 and BSD 2-Clause) and of the Bodleian Libraries'
            consolidated TEI schema (BSD 2-Clause), and its compiled Schematron the code of SchXslt2 (David Maus,
            MIT): their notices are at the top of each generated file.</licence>
        </availability>
      </publicationStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <p>Written for the project, on TEI P5 and the Bodleian's consolidated schema for manuscript
          descriptions.</p>
      </sourceDesc>
    </fileDesc>
    <encodingDesc>
      <classDecl>
        <taxonomy xml:id="tiers">
          <desc>The tiers: how far a file goes, from a minimal file to the full encoding. Every element, attribute
            and rule of the schema belongs to one tier, named by <att>corresp</att> on its specification, or, for an
            element taken from TEI unchanged, by the table of elements beside the specification.</desc>
          <category xml:id="tier-required">
            <catDesc><term>required</term>: what every file has. A file without it fails the checks: the import
              refuses a file that fails the RelaxNG, and reports the Schematron's errors, such as a formal title
              without the document's code.</catDesc>
          </category>
          <category xml:id="tier-common">
            <catDesc><term>common</term>: what most encoders add, as most of the project's coded files
              do.</catDesc>
          </category>
          <category xml:id="tier-full">
            <catDesc><term>full</term>: every other claim about the text, its source or the world, at full depth,
              signed and with its evidence.</catDesc>
          </category>
          <category xml:id="tier-export-only">
            <catDesc><term>export only</term>: the application's own state, which only its exports write, so that
              anyone can read them.</catDesc>
          </category>
        </taxonomy>
      </classDecl>
    </encodingDesc>
  </teiHeader>
  <text>
    <front>
      <div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="introduction">
  <head>The Solemne TEI schema</head>
  <p>The schema of the TEI files the application imports and exports: early medieval canon law texts, their
    structure, what is marked in them, and the records they refer to. It is generated into RelaxNG, which the
    import requires, and Schematron, whose findings the import reports and the exports must pass.</p>
</div>
    </front>
    <body>
      <div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="what-a-file-describes" n="I">
  <head>What a file describes</head>
  <p>This part's prose comes in a later version of the guide.</p>
</div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron" xml:id="file-and-header" n="II">
  <head>The file and its header</head>
  <p>The title statement opens with a formal title holding the document's identifiers, once each: its code,
    in an <gi>idno</gi> without a type (<code>C.NIC-0325</code>); its category, typed
    <val>category</val> (<val>SYSCOLL</val>, <val>CHRCOLL</val>, <val>C</val>, <val>D</val>, <val>P</val>,
    <val>H</val>, <val>EX</val>, <val>EP</val>, <val>LR</val>, <val>CPT</val>, <val>CHA</val> or
    <val>UNK</val>); and its type, typed <val>type</val> (<val>edition</val>, <val>manuscript</val>,
    <val>reconstruction</val>, <val>hypothesis</val> or <val>placeholder</val>). The code begins with its
    category's prefix: <code>COLL</code> for both kinds of collection, the category itself for the others;
    <val>UNK</val>, and <val>LR</val>, <val>CPT</val> and <val>CHA</val>, whose prefixes aren't decided yet,
    take any. A manuscript's code (<code>COLL.Dach.ms-Brn-Burg-425</code>), like a document typed
    <val>manuscript</val>, goes with the manuscript's description in the <gi>sourceDesc</gi>. An export adds
    the permalink of each level the file belongs to, typed <val>work</val>, <val>version</val>,
    <val>witness</val> or <val>transcription</val>. Further titles are aliases or other titles. Dates are given as one point
    (<att>when</att>) or as a span with both bounds. Persons, places and events listed in the standOff
    either point to a record or describe one.</p>
  <p>The header points to records as the text does, by <att>ref</att> in the same forms: a title to its
    work, an author or an editor to a person, a country, region, settlement, place of origin, repository or
    institution to its record, and the names (<gi>persName</gi>, <gi>orgName</gi>, <gi>placeName</gi>) to
    theirs. <gi>provenance</gi>, <gi>acquisition</gi> and <gi>origin</gi> have no <att>ref</att> in TEI: the
    record they point to is named inside them, by a name with <att>ref</att>, and the import makes the
    relation from that name. <att>key</att> and <att>corresp</att> keep TEI's other uses; a record's pointer
    in them is reported.</p>
  <p>A manuscript is described, for now, after the Bodleian's consolidated schema, with at least one
    codicological unit (<gi>msPart</gi>) in every description, each with its own identifier: the manuscript
    holds its identity and its binding, a unit its physical description, its date, its hands and its
    decoration.</p>
  <p>A node's ids in other projects (SCTA's, the Clavis canonum's keys) are given in <att>sameAs</att>, each
    with a prefix declared in the header by a <gi>prefixDef</gi> in <gi>listPrefixDef</gi>
    (<code>clavis:IS35.27</code>). The application knows four: <code>scta</code> (SCTA,
    <code>http://scta.info/resource/…</code>), <code>clavis</code> (the Clavis canonum,
    <code>https://data.mgh.de/databases/clavis/db/legacysearch?key=…</code>), <code>pseudoisidor</code> (the
    Pseudoisidor project) and <code>corpuscorporum</code> (the Corpus Corporum's Patrologia Latina); another
    may be declared, and is reported. A prefix used without its declaration is an error. A record's or a
    manuscript's ids are <gi>idno</gi>s typed by their authority, from a closed list, beside the kinds of
    identifier the files use: <val>shelfmark</val>, <val>ISBN</val>, <val>url</val>,
    <val>biblatex</val>.</p>

  <p>Counter-examples of this part's rules: each breaks the rule its <att>n</att> names.</p>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="title-first-formal">
    <titleStmt>
      <title type="alias">Council of Samplia, 600</title>
      <title type="formal">
        <idno>C.SAM-0600</idno>
        <idno type="category">C</idno>
        <idno type="type">edition</idno>
      </title>
    </titleStmt>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="title-one-formal">
    <titleStmt>
      <title type="formal">
        <idno>C.SAM-0600</idno>
        <idno type="category">C</idno>
        <idno type="type">edition</idno>
      </title>
      <title type="formal">Council of Samplia</title>
    </titleStmt>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="title-type">
    <title type="main">Council of Samplia, 600</title>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="title-alias-words">
    <title type="alias"/>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="title-other-source">
    <title type="other">Synodus Sampliensis</title>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="formal-title-idnos">
    <title type="formal">
      <idno>C.SAM-0600</idno>
      <idno type="category">C</idno>
    </title>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="idno-in-formal-title">
    <title type="alias">Council of Samplia, 600 <idno>C.SAM-0600</idno></title>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="idno-type">
    <title type="formal">
      <idno>C.SAM-0600</idno>
      <idno type="category">C</idno>
      <idno type="type">edition</idno>
      <idno type="shelfmark">MS 12</idno>
    </title>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="code-format">
    <title type="formal">
      <idno>C.SAM_0600</idno>
      <idno type="category">C</idno>
      <idno type="type">edition</idno>
    </title>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="code-category">
    <title type="formal">
      <idno>C.SAM-0600</idno>
      <idno type="category">D</idno>
      <idno type="type">edition</idno>
    </title>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="category-value">
    <title type="formal">
      <idno>CAN.SAM-0600</idno>
      <idno type="category">CAN</idno>
      <idno type="type">edition</idno>
    </title>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="document-type-value">
    <title type="formal">
      <idno>C.SAM-0600</idno>
      <idno type="category">C</idno>
      <idno type="type">copy</idno>
    </title>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="code-manuscript">
    <title type="formal">
      <idno>COLL.Samp.ms-Now-NL-12</idno>
      <idno type="category">SYSCOLL</idno>
      <idno type="type">edition</idno>
    </title>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="type-manuscript">
    <title type="formal">
      <idno>C.SAM-0600</idno>
      <idno type="category">C</idno>
      <idno type="type">manuscript</idno>
    </title>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="idno-type-unknown">
    <sourceDesc>
      <bibl>
        <title>Concilia exempli gratia</title>
        <idno type="isbn">0-000-00000-0</idno><!-- breaks the rule -->
      </bibl>
    </sourceDesc>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="record-pointer-in-ref">
    <sourceDesc>
      <bibl>
        <author key="#new_person_Exemplus">Exemplus</author>
        <title>Epistolae</title>
      </bibl>
    </sourceDesc>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="record-pointer-form">
    <sourceDesc>
      <bibl>
        <author ref="new_person_Exemplus">Exemplus</author><!-- breaks the rule -->
        <title>Epistolae</title>
      </bibl>
    </sourceDesc>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="same-as-prefix-declared">
    <div type="chapter" n="1" sameAs="clavis:IS01.01">
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <head type="rubric">De episcopis.</head>
      <p>Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis maneant.</p>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="prefix-known">
    <listPrefixDef>
      <prefixDef ident="unknown" matchPattern="(.+)" replacementPattern="https://example.org/$1">
        <p>An identifier of a project the application doesn't know.</p>
      </prefixDef>
    </listPrefixDef>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="correction-default">
    <editorialDecl>
      <correction xml:id="checked-against-the-edition" status="high">
        <p>Checked against the edition.</p>
      </correction>
      <correction xml:id="not-checked-yet" status="low">
        <p>Not checked yet.</p>
      </correction>
    </editorialDecl>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="decls-target">
    <editorialDecl>
      <correction xml:id="checked" status="high">
        <p>Checked against the edition.</p>
      </correction>
    </editorialDecl>
    <div type="chapter" n="1" decls="#unchecked">
      <p>Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis maneant.</p>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="inferred-units-pointed-to">
    <editorialDecl>
      <segmentation xml:id="inferred-in-some-chapters" type="inferred-units" default="false">
        <p>The units of reception aren't marked in some chapters: each is one.</p>
      </segmentation>
    </editorialDecl>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="segmentation-type-unknown">
    <editorialDecl>
      <segmentation type="units-inferred"><!-- breaks the rule -->
        <p>Units inferred.</p>
      </segmentation>
    </editorialDecl>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="code-matches-file-name">
    <!-- file name: C.SAM-0601.xml -->
    <TEI>
      <teiHeader>
        <fileDesc>
          <titleStmt>
            <title type="formal">
              <idno>C.SAM-0600</idno>
              <idno type="category">C</idno>
              <idno type="type">edition</idno>
            </title>
          </titleStmt>
          <publicationStmt>
            <p>An example of the guide.</p>
          </publicationStmt>
          <sourceDesc>
            <p>An excerpt.</p>
          </sourceDesc>
        </fileDesc>
      </teiHeader>
      <text>
        <body/>
      </text>
    </TEI>
  </egXML>

  <specGrp xml:id="file-and-header-specs">
    <!-- The title statement: the formal title first, then aliases and other titles. -->
    <elementSpec ident="titleStmt" module="header" mode="change" corresp="#tier-required">
      <constraintSpec ident="title-first-formal" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-required">
        <desc>The title statement opens with the formal title.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt">
            <sch:assert id="title-first-formal" test="tei:title[1][@type = 'formal']">The title statement opens
              with a title typed formal.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="title-one-formal" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-required">
        <desc>The title statement has one formal title.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt">
            <sch:assert id="title-one-formal" test="count(tei:title[@type = 'formal']) = 1">The title statement
              has one formal title.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="title-type" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-required">
        <desc>The title statement's titles are typed formal, alias or other.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt/tei:title">
            <sch:assert id="title-type" test="@type = ('formal', 'alias', 'other')">A title in the title statement
              is typed formal, alias or other.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="title-alias-words" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-common">
        <desc>An alias isn't empty.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt/tei:title">
            <sch:assert id="title-alias-words" test="not(@type = 'alias') or normalize-space(.) != ''">An alias
              isn't empty.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="title-other-source" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A title typed other names its source.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt/tei:title">
            <sch:assert id="title-other-source" role="warning" test="not(@type = 'other') or @source">A title
              typed other names its source in @source.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
    </elementSpec>

    <!-- The formal title's identifiers: the document's code, its category and its type; an export's levels. -->
    <elementSpec ident="idno" module="header" mode="change" corresp="#tier-required">
      <constraintSpec ident="formal-title-idnos" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-required">
        <desc>The formal title holds the document's code (an identifier without a type), its category and its
          type, once each; an export adds the permalinks of the levels the file belongs to.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt/tei:title[@type = 'formal']">
            <sch:assert id="formal-title-idnos" test="count(tei:idno[not(@type)]) = 1 and count(tei:idno[@type =               'category']) = 1 and count(tei:idno[@type = 'type']) = 1 and (every $level in ('work', 'version',               'witness', 'transcription') satisfies count(tei:idno[@type = $level]) le 1)">The formal title holds
              the document's code (an identifier without a type), its category and its type, once each, and at
              most one permalink for each level the file belongs to.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="idno-in-formal-title" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-required">
        <desc>An identifier in the title statement stands in the formal title.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt/tei:title/tei:idno">
            <sch:assert id="idno-in-formal-title" test="parent::tei:title[@type = 'formal']">An identifier in the
              title statement stands in the formal title.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="idno-type" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-required">
        <desc>An identifier in the title statement is the code, the category, the type, or a level's
          permalink.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt/tei:title/tei:idno">
            <sch:assert id="idno-type" test="not(@type) or @type = ('category', 'type', 'work', 'version',               'witness', 'transcription')">An identifier in the formal title is the code (without a type), the
              category, the type, or the permalink of a level (work, version, witness, transcription).</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="code-format" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-required">
        <desc>The document's code is a prefix of capitals, a dot, then letters and digits joined by dots or
          hyphens.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt/tei:title[@type = 'formal']/tei:idno[not(@type)]">
            <sch:assert id="code-format" test="matches(normalize-space(.),               '^[A-Z]+\.[A-Za-z0-9]+([.\-][A-Za-z0-9]+)*$')">The document's code (<sch:value-of select="normalize-space(.)"/>) begins with its category's prefix and a dot, and holds only letters,
              digits, dots and hyphens.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="code-category" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-required">
        <desc>The document's code begins with its category's prefix: COLL for both kinds of collection, the
          category itself for the others; UNK's any.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt/tei:title[@type = 'formal']/tei:idno[not(@type)]">
            <sch:let name="category" value="normalize-space(../tei:idno[@type = 'category'][1])"/>
            <sch:let name="prefix" value="substring-before(normalize-space(.), '.')"/>
            <sch:assert id="code-category" test="$category = ('', 'UNK') or $prefix = (if               ($category = ('SYSCOLL', 'CHRCOLL')) then 'COLL' else $category)">The document's code
              (<sch:value-of select="normalize-space(.)"/>) begins with its category's prefix (<sch:value-of select="if ($category = ('SYSCOLL', 'CHRCOLL')) then 'COLL' else $category"/>, for the category
              <sch:value-of select="$category"/>).</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="code-manuscript" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A manuscript's code goes with the manuscript's description.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt/tei:title[@type = 'formal']/tei:idno[not(@type)]">
            <sch:assert id="code-manuscript" test="not(contains(normalize-space(.), '.ms-')) or               ancestor::tei:fileDesc/tei:sourceDesc//tei:msDesc">A manuscript's code (<sch:value-of select="normalize-space(.)"/>) goes with the manuscript's description (msDesc) in the
              sourceDesc.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="code-matches-file-name" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-required">
        <desc>A file named by a code, any category's, is named by its document's code.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt/tei:title[@type = 'formal']/tei:idno[not(@type)]">
            <sch:assert id="code-matches-file-name" role="warning" test="not(matches(base-uri(.),               '/[A-Z]+\.[^/]*\.xml$')) or ends-with(base-uri(.), concat('/',               encode-for-uri(normalize-space(.)), '.xml'))">A file named by a code is named by its document's code
              (<sch:value-of select="normalize-space(.)"/>).</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="category-value" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-required">
        <desc>The document's category is one of the categories.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt/tei:title[@type = 'formal']/tei:idno[@type = 'category']">
            <sch:assert id="category-value" test="normalize-space(.) = ('SYSCOLL', 'CHRCOLL', 'C', 'D', 'P', 'H',               'EX', 'EP', 'LR', 'CPT', 'CHA', 'UNK')">The document's category (<sch:value-of select="normalize-space(.)"/>) is one of SYSCOLL, CHRCOLL, C, D, P, H, EX, EP, LR, CPT, CHA,
              UNK.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="document-type-value" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-required">
        <desc>The document's type is one of the types.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt/tei:title[@type = 'formal']/tei:idno[@type = 'type']">
            <sch:assert id="document-type-value" test="normalize-space(.) = ('edition', 'manuscript',               'reconstruction', 'hypothesis', 'placeholder')">The document's type (<sch:value-of select="normalize-space(.)"/>) is one of edition, manuscript, reconstruction, hypothesis,
              placeholder.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="type-manuscript" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A document typed manuscript has the manuscript's description.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:fileDesc/tei:titleStmt/tei:title[@type = 'formal']/tei:idno[@type = 'type']">
            <sch:assert id="type-manuscript" test="not(normalize-space(.) = 'manuscript') or               ancestor::tei:fileDesc/tei:sourceDesc//tei:msDesc">A document typed manuscript has the manuscript's
              description (msDesc) in its sourceDesc.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="type" mode="change" corresp="#tier-required">
          <valList type="closed" mode="replace" xml:id="idno-type-unknown" corresp="#tier-required">
            <valItem ident="category">
              <desc>in the formal title: the document's category</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="type">
              <desc>in the formal title: the document's type</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="work">
              <desc>in an export's formal title: the permalink of the work the file belongs to</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="version">
              <desc>in an export's formal title: the permalink of the version</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="witness">
              <desc>in an export's formal title: the permalink of the witness</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="transcription">
              <desc>in an export's formal title: the permalink of the transcription</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="wikidata">
              <desc>Wikidata's item (Q…)</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="viaf">
              <desc>the Virtual International Authority File</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="gnd">
              <desc>the Gemeinsame Normdatei</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="geonames">
              <desc>GeoNames</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="tgn">
              <desc>the Getty Thesaurus of Geographic Names</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="pleiades">
              <desc>Pleiades, for ancient places</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="mirabile">
              <desc>Mirabile</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="clavis">
              <desc>the Clavis canonum</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="biblissima">
              <desc>Biblissima</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="schoenberg">
              <desc>the Schoenberg Database of Manuscripts</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="hmml">
              <desc>the Hill Museum &amp; Manuscript Library</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="bodleian">
              <desc>the Bodleian Libraries' catalogues</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="manusOnline">
              <desc>Manus Online</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="ieArk">
              <desc>the Bodleian's ARK for an intellectual entity</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="crArk">
              <desc>the Bodleian's ARK for a catalogue record</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="SCN">
              <desc>the Bodleian's Summary Catalogue number</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="shelfmark">
              <desc>a manuscript's shelfmark</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="ISBN">
              <desc>a publication's ISBN</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="url">
              <desc>an address on the web</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="biblatex">
              <desc>a publication's biblatex key</desc>
            </valItem>
          </valList>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>

    <!-- The header points to records the same way: titles to works, authors and editors to persons, places
         and institutions to theirs. provenance, acquisition and origin have no @ref in TEI: the record they
         point to is named inside them, by a name with @ref. -->
    <elementSpec ident="title" module="core" mode="change" corresp="#tier-required">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
    <elementSpec ident="author" module="core" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
    <elementSpec ident="editor" module="core" mode="change" corresp="#tier-common">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>

    <elementSpec ident="teiHeader" module="header" mode="change" corresp="#tier-required">
      <constraintSpec ident="record-pointer-in-ref" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A record is pointed to by @ref, not by @key or @corresp.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:*[@key or @corresp]">
            <sch:report id="record-pointer-in-ref" role="warning" test="some $p in               tokenize(normalize-space(string-join((@key, @corresp), ' ')), ' ') satisfies matches($p,               '^#?[Nn]ew_[A-Za-z]+_|^#?(PERS\.\d+|solemne_person_\d+)$|^https?://\S+/id/(person|place|institution|event|manuscript|publication)/')">&lt;<sch:name/>&gt;
              points to a record in @key or @corresp (<sch:value-of select="normalize-space(string-join((@key,               @corresp), ' '))"/>): a record is pointed to by @ref, on a name inside provenance, acquisition and
              origin.</sch:report>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
    </elementSpec>

    <!-- External ids: a node's in @sameAs, its prefix declared in the header; a record's or a manuscript's in an
         idno typed by its authority. -->
    <elementSpec ident="prefixDef" module="header" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <constraintSpec ident="same-as-prefix-declared" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A prefix used in @sameAs is declared in the header.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:*[@sameAs]">
            <sch:let name="declared" value="/tei:TEI/tei:teiHeader//tei:prefixDef/@ident"/>
            <sch:assert id="same-as-prefix-declared" test="every $id in tokenize(normalize-space(@sameAs), ' ')               satisfies (not(matches($id, '^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.\-]*:')) or matches($id, '^https?:') or               substring-before($id, ':') = $declared)">The prefixes in @sameAs (<sch:value-of select="normalize-space(@sameAs)"/>) are declared in the header, by prefixDef in
              listPrefixDef.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="prefix-known" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>The prefixes the application knows are scta, clavis, pseudoisidor and corpuscorporum.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:prefixDef">
            <sch:assert id="prefix-known" role="warning" test="@ident = ('scta', 'clavis', 'pseudoisidor',               'corpuscorporum')">The prefix <sch:value-of select="@ident"/> isn't one the application knows (scta,
              clavis, pseudoisidor, corpuscorporum).</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
    </elementSpec>

    <!-- The declarations a text and its parts point to: curation and inferred units. -->
    <elementSpec ident="editorialDecl" module="header" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <constraintSpec ident="decls-target" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>@decls points to a correction or a segmentation in the header.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:*[@decls]">
            <sch:assert id="decls-target" test="every $t in tokenize(normalize-space(@decls), ' ') satisfies               (starts-with($t, '#') and exists(/tei:TEI/tei:teiHeader//(tei:correction |               tei:segmentation)[@xml:id = substring($t, 2)]))">@decls (<sch:value-of select="normalize-space(@decls)"/>) points to a correction or a segmentation in the
              header.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="correction-default" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>Of several corrections, one is the default.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:editorialDecl[count(tei:correction) gt 1]">
            <sch:assert id="correction-default" test="count(tei:correction[@default = 'true']) = 1">Of several
              corrections, one is the default (@default="true"): the whole text's.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="inferred-units-pointed-to" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A statement of inferred units for some divisions is pointed to by them.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:segmentation[@type = 'inferred-units'][@default = 'false']">
            <sch:let name="id" value="concat('#', @xml:id)"/>
            <sch:assert id="inferred-units-pointed-to" role="warning" test="@xml:id and               //@decls[tokenize(normalize-space(.), ' ') = $id]">A statement of inferred units for some divisions
              (@default="false") is pointed to by their @decls.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
    </elementSpec>

    <!-- The units of reception, where the encoders didn't mark them. -->
    <elementSpec ident="segmentation" module="header" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <classes mode="change">
        <memberOf key="att.typed"/>
      </classes>
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="type" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <valList type="closed" mode="replace" xml:id="segmentation-type-unknown" corresp="#tier-full">
            <valItem ident="inferred-units">
              <desc>the units of reception aren't marked: each division that holds paragraphs is one</desc>
            </valItem>
          </valList>
        </attDef>
        <attDef ident="subtype" mode="delete"/>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
  </specGrp>
</div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron" xml:id="text" n="III">
  <head>The text</head>
  <p>A document is a tree of divisions. A division holds headings, then either paragraphs or divisions,
    never both; headings may stand where the encoding puts them, usually first. Page breaks, notes and gaps
    may stand between them. The body itself, the document's root, follows the same rule.</p>
  <p>Every division and heading has a type, from a closed list, so that a misspelled type fails. A numbered
    division carries its number as a value in <att>n</att> (49 for a heading XLVIIII; 11a for a chapter
    after 11), and its number heading keeps the number as written. A unit is a subdivision without a
    heading of its own, written only where units stand side by side: a division whose text is one unit
    holds its paragraphs itself.</p>
  <p>The paragraphs of a division that holds no divisions are one unit of reception. Where the encoders
    didn't mark the units, the header says so once, in <gi>segmentation</gi> with the type
    <val>inferred-units</val>: for the whole file, when it's the default (<att>default</att> true) or stands
    alone; or, declared with <att>default</att> false and an id, for the divisions that point to it by
    <att>decls</att>, where only a few are unmarked among many units. A statement for divisions that none
    points to is reported.</p>
  <p>How far a text has been checked is its curation, given by <gi>correction</gi> in
    <gi>editorialDecl</gi>, its <att>status</att> <val>high</val>, <val>medium</val>, <val>low</val> or
    <val>unknown</val>, and a paragraph saying how, which TEI requires: the whole text's value is the
    default; a division or a paragraph that differs points
    to another <gi>correction</gi> by <att>decls</att>. Of several corrections, one is the default.
    <att>decls</att> on the text, the body, a division or a paragraph points only to a <gi>correction</gi>
    or a <gi>segmentation</gi> in the header. What was left out by choice is said once, in
    <gi>samplingDecl</gi>; completeness is never stated, but read from the gaps.</p>


  <p>Counter-examples of this part's rules: each breaks the rule its <att>n</att> names.</p>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="division-holds-paragraphs-and-divisions">
    <div type="chapter" n="1"><!-- breaks the rule -->
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <head type="rubric">De episcopis.</head>
      <p>Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis maneant.</p>
      <div type="unit">
        <p>Et clerici.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="division-type-missing">
    <div n="1"><!-- breaks the rule -->
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <head type="rubric">De episcopis.</head>
      <p>Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis maneant.</p>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="division-type-misspelled">
    <div type="chpater" n="1"><!-- breaks the rule -->
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <head type="rubric">De episcopis.</head>
      <p>Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis maneant.</p>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="division-number-not-a-value">
    <div type="chapter" n="I"><!-- breaks the rule -->
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <head type="rubric">De episcopis.</head>
      <p>Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis maneant.</p>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="number-heading-n">
    <div type="chapter">
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <head type="rubric">De episcopis.</head>
      <p>Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis maneant.</p>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="heading-type-missing">
    <div type="chapter" n="1">
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <head>De episcopis.</head><!-- breaks the rule -->
      <p>Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis maneant.</p>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="heading-type-misspelled">
    <div type="chapter" n="1">
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <head type="inscripto">De episcopis.</head><!-- breaks the rule -->
      <p>Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis maneant.</p>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="unit-alone">
    <div type="chapter" n="1">
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <head type="rubric">De episcopis.</head>
      <div type="unit">
        <p>Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis maneant.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="unit-holds-text">
    <div type="chapter" n="1">
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <head type="rubric">De episcopis.</head>
      <div type="unit">
        <head type="rubric">De eodem.</head>
        <p>Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis maneant.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="unit">
        <p>Et clerici.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="register-item-in-register">
    <div type="registerItem" n="2">
      <head type="number">II.</head>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="page-break-without-number">
    <p>Placuit ut episcopi<pb/><!-- breaks the rule --> in ciuitatibus suis maneant.</p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="gap-reason-unknown">
    <p>Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis maneant. <gap reason="missing"/><!-- breaks the rule --></p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="gap-unit-unknown">
    <p>Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis maneant. <gap reason="lacuna" quantity="2" unit="folios"/><!-- breaks the rule --></p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="gap-quantity-unit">
    <p>Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis maneant. <gap reason="lacuna" quantity="2"/></p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="text-elements">
    <p>Placuit ut episcopi <orgName>ecclesiae</orgName> maneant.</p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="element-outside-the-schema">
    <p>Placuit ut <hi rend="italic">episcopi</hi> maneant.</p><!-- breaks the rule -->
  </egXML>

  <specGrp xml:id="text-specs">
    <!-- The structure of the text. -->
    <macroSpec ident="solemne.structure" mode="add" xml:id="division-holds-paragraphs-and-divisions" corresp="#tier-required">
      <desc>What a division or the body holds: headings with either paragraphs or divisions, never both, and page
        breaks, notes and gaps between them.</desc>
      <content>
        <alternate>
          <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <elementRef key="head"/>
            <macroRef key="solemne.between"/>
            <elementRef key="p"/>
          </alternate>
          <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <elementRef key="head"/>
            <macroRef key="solemne.between"/>
            <elementRef key="div"/>
          </alternate>
        </alternate>
      </content>
    </macroSpec>
    <macroSpec ident="solemne.between" mode="add">
      <desc>What may stand between headings, paragraphs and divisions.</desc>
      <content>
        <alternate>
          <elementRef key="pb"/>
          <elementRef key="note"/>
          <elementRef key="gap"/>
        </alternate>
      </content>
    </macroSpec>

    <elementSpec ident="body" module="textstructure" mode="change" corresp="#tier-required">
      <content>
        <macroRef key="solemne.structure"/>
      </content>
      <constraintSpec ident="text-elements" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-required">
        <desc>Inside the text, only the annotation layers' elements.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:body//tei:*">
            <sch:assert id="text-elements" test="local-name() = ('div', 'head', 'p', 'note', 'pb', 'lb', 'gap',               'persName', 'placeName', 'eventName', 'bibl', 'cit', 'quote', 'ref', 'seg', 'date', 'subst', 'add',               'del', 'unclear', 'foreign', 'choice', 'corr', 'sic', 'abbr', 'expan', 'supplied', 'rs',               'anchor')">&lt;<sch:name/>&gt; isn't one of the text's elements.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
    </elementSpec>

    <elementSpec ident="div" module="textstructure" mode="change" corresp="#tier-common">
      <content>
        <macroRef key="solemne.structure"/>
      </content>
      <constraintSpec ident="unit-alone" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>Units are written only where they stand side by side.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:div[@type = 'unit']">
            <sch:assert id="unit-alone" test="count(../tei:div) gt 1">A unit stands alone in its division: its
              paragraphs belong to the division itself.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="unit-holds-text" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A unit holds paragraphs only.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:div[@type = 'unit']">
            <sch:assert id="unit-holds-text" test="not(tei:div) and not(tei:head)">A unit holds paragraphs only,
              without headings or divisions.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="register-item-in-register" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A register's items stand in a register.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:div[@type = 'registerItem']">
            <sch:assert id="register-item-in-register" test="parent::tei:div[@type = 'register']">A register item
              stands in a register.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="number-heading-n" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-common">
        <desc>A division with a number heading carries the number as a value.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:div[tei:head[@type = 'number']]">
            <sch:assert id="number-heading-n" test="@n">A division with a number heading
              (<sch:value-of select="normalize-space(tei:head[@type = 'number'][1])"/>) has @n.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="req" xml:id="division-type-missing" corresp="#tier-common">
          <valList type="closed" mode="replace" xml:id="division-type-misspelled" corresp="#tier-common">
            <valItem ident="section">
              <desc>a book, a part, or one text inside a document (a council in a collection)</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="chapter">
              <desc>a numbered or titled unit; chapters may hold chapters</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="unit">
              <desc>a subdivision without a heading of its own, where several stand side by side: a norm and its
                authority statements, one signatory among the subscriptions</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="preface"/>
            <valItem ident="closer">
              <desc>a closing rubric, or a letter's farewell and date</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="subscriptions">
              <desc>the signatories</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="register">
              <desc>the list of chapter titles</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="registerItem">
              <desc>one entry of a register</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="part">
              <desc>a part of Gratian's Decretum</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="distinctio">
              <desc>a distinction of Gratian's Decretum</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="causa">
              <desc>a causa of Gratian's Decretum</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="quaestio">
              <desc>a question of a causa</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="capitulum">
              <desc>a canon of Gratian's Decretum</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="dictum">
              <desc>Gratian's own words between the canons</desc>
            </valItem>
          </valList>
        </attDef>
        <attDef ident="n" mode="change" corresp="#tier-common">
          <desc>the division's number, as a value: 49 for a heading XLVIIII; a letter after it for a chapter after a
            numbered one, or for a number repeated</desc>
          <datatype xml:id="division-number-not-a-value" corresp="#tier-common">
            <dataRef name="token" restriction="[0-9]+[a-z]?"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
        <attDef ident="subtype" mode="delete"/>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>

    <elementSpec ident="head" module="core" mode="change" corresp="#tier-common">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="req" xml:id="heading-type-missing" corresp="#tier-common">
          <valList type="closed" mode="replace" xml:id="heading-type-misspelled" corresp="#tier-common">
            <valItem ident="number">
              <desc>the division's number as written ("Cap. II.")</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="rubric">
              <desc>what the text is about ("De subintroductis mulieribus")</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="inscription">
              <desc>where the text comes from ("Ex concilio Nicaeno"), even when it goes on with its subject</desc>
            </valItem>
          </valList>
        </attDef>
        <attDef ident="subtype" mode="delete"/>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>

    <elementSpec ident="pb" module="core" mode="change" corresp="#tier-common">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="n" mode="change" usage="req" xml:id="page-break-without-number" corresp="#tier-common">
          <desc>the page, folio or column: 255, 120ra, 0187A</desc>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>

    <!-- Gaps: why the text is missing, and how much, where known. -->
    <elementSpec ident="gap" module="core" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <constraintSpec ident="gap-quantity-unit" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A gap's quantity is given with its unit.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:gap[@quantity or @unit]">
            <sch:assert id="gap-quantity-unit" test="@quantity and @unit">A gap's quantity is given with its unit
              (leaves, lines, words or chars), and a unit with its quantity.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="reason" mode="change" usage="opt" corresp="#tier-full">
          <desc>why the text is missing; without a reason, it's unknown</desc>
          <valList type="closed" mode="replace" xml:id="gap-reason-unknown" corresp="#tier-full">
            <valItem ident="lacuna">
              <desc>the witness lacks the text: lost leaves, or a lacuna in the edition it comes from</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="damage">
              <desc>the support is damaged where the text stood</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="illegible">
              <desc>the text can't be read (unclear is for what can be half read)</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="reproduction">
              <desc>the text can't be read in the images or the film used</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="deleted">
              <desc>struck out, and not readable</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="sampling">
              <desc>not transcribed, by the encoder's choice: an incipit and an explicit only</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="editorial">
              <desc>left out for another reason, given in a note</desc>
            </valItem>
          </valList>
        </attDef>
        <attDef ident="unit" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <desc>the unit of the gap's quantity</desc>
          <valList type="closed" mode="replace" xml:id="gap-unit-unknown" corresp="#tier-full">
            <valItem ident="leaves"/>
            <valItem ident="lines"/>
            <valItem ident="words"/>
            <valItem ident="chars">
              <desc>characters</desc>
            </valItem>
          </valList>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
  </specGrp>
</div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron" xml:id="marked-in-the-text" n="IV">
  <head>What is marked in the text</head>
  <p>Inside the body, only the elements of the annotation layers appear: names of persons, places and
    events; works named; statements with their reference and quotation; formulas; dates; notes of three
    types (sources, parallels, editorial remarks); scribal changes; what is unclear or missing; page and
    line breaks; other languages; and editorial corrections. For the rare doubtful cases, an editor's
    addition is <gi>supplied</gi>, and an abbreviation with its expansion a <gi>choice</gi> of
    <gi>abbr</gi> and <gi>expan</gi>. A record of a kind no name element fits is <gi>rs</gi>, its kind in
    <att>type</att> and its record in <att>ref</att>, in the names' forms; a point that a stand-off
    annotation refers to is an <gi>anchor</gi>. A span that crosses others or the structure, such as a
    quotation over several paragraphs, is split into fragments, each nesting where it stands, joined by
    <att>next</att> and <att>prev</att>, which point to each other.</p>
  <p>A quotation and a note point to their sources in <att>source</att>, in one of these forms: a document's
    code (<code>C.NIC-0325</code>), alone or with a citation after an underscore
    (<code>C.NIC-0325_3</code>, <code>COLL.Dach.ms-Brn-Burg-425_2.49</code>); a Bible reference, by one
    code per book, chapter and verse (<code>MAT_18_19</code>, <code>PHP_3_17-20</code>); a work by its
    Gryson siglum, with the place cited (<code>IS_ety_1.2.3</code>); or an SCTA resource. A loose reference
    starts with <code>cf_</code>. Names point to their records by placeholders (<code>#new_person_…</code>)
    until the import resolves them, then by permalinks.</p>
  <p>A gap may say why the text is missing, in <att>reason</att>: <val>lacuna</val> (the witness lacks
    it: lost leaves, or a lacuna in the edition it comes from), <val>damage</val>, <val>illegible</val>
    (<gi>unclear</gi> is for what can be half read), <val>reproduction</val> (not readable in the images or
    the film used), <val>deleted</val> (struck out and not readable), <val>sampling</val> (not transcribed,
    by the encoder's choice: an incipit and an explicit only) or <val>editorial</val> (left out for another
    reason, given in a note); without a reason, it's unknown. Its extent, where known, is a
    <att>quantity</att> with its <att>unit</att> (<val>leaves</val>, <val>lines</val>, <val>words</val>,
    <val>chars</val>), or <att>extent</att> in words.</p>

  <p>Counter-examples of this part's rules: each breaks the rule its <att>n</att> names.</p>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="text-note-type">
    <p>Placuit ut episcopi maneant.<note type="links">See elsewhere.</note></p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="note-has-content">
    <p>Placuit ut episcopi maneant.<note type="editorial"/></p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="note-type-misspelled">
    <p>Placuit ut episcopi maneant.<note type="souce" source="C.NIC-0325_3"/><!-- breaks the rule --></p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="source-note-codes">
    <p>Placuit ut episcopi maneant.<note type="source">C.NIC-0325_15</note></p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="source-pointer-form">
    <p>Placuit ut episcopi maneant.<note type="source" source="CNIC.325.2"/><!-- breaks the rule: an older code --></p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="source-pointer-form">
    <p>Placuit ut episcopi maneant.<note type="source" source="C.NIC_0325_3"/><!-- breaks the rule: an underscore in the code --></p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="source-pointer-form">
    <cit><ref>Dominus ait:</ref> <quote source="MATT_5_3">Beati pauperes</quote><!-- breaks the rule: no such book --></cit>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="source-pointer-form">
    <cit><ref>Apostolus ait:</ref> <quote source="1CO_9_14f">qui euangelium adnuntiant</quote><!-- breaks the rule: no such verse --></cit>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="quotation-typed">
    <cit><ref>Apostolus ait:</ref> <quote type="ROM_12_5">unum corpus sumus</quote><!-- breaks the rule --></cit>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="reference-type-unknown">
    <cit><ref type="paratext">Dominus ait:</ref><!-- breaks the rule --> <quote source="MAT_5_3">Beati pauperes</quote></cit>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="seg-type-missing">
    <p><seg>Si quis</seg><!-- breaks the rule --> episcopus migrauerit, deponatur.</p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="seg-type-misspelled">
    <p><seg type="fomula">Si quis</seg><!-- breaks the rule --> episcopus migrauerit, deponatur.</p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="record-pointer-form">
    <p>Placuit <persName ref="new_person_Paul">Paulo</persName><!-- breaks the rule --> ut episcopi maneant.</p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="record-pointer-form">
    <p>Placuit ut episcopi per <rs type="diocese" ref="new_diocese_Samplia">dioecesim</rs><!-- breaks the rule --> maneant.</p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="fragment-next">
    <div type="chapter" n="1">
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <p><quote xml:id="next-wrong-a" next="#next-wrong-c">Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis</quote></p>
      <p><quote xml:id="next-wrong-b">maneant.</quote></p>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="fragment-prev">
    <div type="chapter" n="1">
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <p><quote xml:id="prev-wrong-a">Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus suis</quote></p>
      <p><quote xml:id="prev-wrong-b" prev="#prev-wrong-a">maneant.</quote></p>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="fragment-attributes">
    <div type="chapter" n="1">
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <p><quote xml:id="attributes-wrong-a" next="#attributes-wrong-b" source="C.NIC-0325_15">Placuit ut episcopi
          in ciuitatibus suis</quote></p>
      <p><quote xml:id="attributes-wrong-b" prev="#attributes-wrong-a" source="C.NIC-0325_15">maneant.</quote></p>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="fragment-order">
    <div type="chapter" n="1">
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <p><quote xml:id="order-wrong-b" prev="#order-wrong-a">maneant.</quote></p>
      <p><quote xml:id="order-wrong-a" next="#order-wrong-b" source="C.NIC-0325_15">Placuit ut episcopi in
          ciuitatibus suis</quote></p>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <p>Fragments as they should be: a quotation over two paragraphs, its source on the first fragment; a formula over
    two, each fragment typed, as the RelaxNG requires of every segment.</p>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
    <div type="chapter" n="1">
      <head type="number">I.</head>
      <p><quote xml:id="fragments-a" next="#fragments-b" source="C.NIC-0325_15">Placuit ut episcopi in ciuitatibus
          suis</quote></p>
      <p><quote xml:id="fragments-b" prev="#fragments-a">maneant.</quote></p>
    </div>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
    <div type="chapter" n="2">
      <head type="number">II.</head>
      <p>Placuit ut <seg type="formula" xml:id="formula-a" next="#formula-b">si quis</seg></p>
      <p><seg type="formula" xml:id="formula-b" prev="#formula-a">episcopus</seg> migrauerit, deponatur.</p>
    </div>
  </egXML>

  <specGrp xml:id="marked-in-the-text-specs">
    <!-- Notes: in the text, typed by their layer. -->
    <elementSpec ident="note" module="core" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <constraintSpec ident="text-note-type" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>In the text, a note's type is its layer.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:body//tei:note">
            <sch:assert id="text-note-type" test="@type = ('source', 'parallel', 'editorial')">A note in the text
              is typed source, parallel or editorial.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="note-has-content" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A note holds words, or its codes in source.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:note">
            <sch:assert id="note-has-content" test="normalize-space(.) != '' or @source or *">A note holds words,
              or its codes in @source.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="source-note-codes" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A source note's codes are in source, not in its words.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:body//tei:note[@type = 'source']">
            <sch:report id="source-note-codes" role="warning" test="some $w in tokenize(normalize-space(.),               '[\s;,]+') satisfies matches($w,               '^(cf_)?((C|D|COLL|P|EP|H|EX|W)\.[A-Za-z0-9.\-]+(_[A-Za-z0-9.\-]+)?|[1-4]?[A-Z]{2,4}_[0-9]+(_[0-9]+)?(-[0-9]+)?)$')">A
              source note's words hold a code (<sch:value-of select="normalize-space(.)"/>): it belongs in
              @source.</sch:report>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="type" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <valList type="closed" mode="replace" xml:id="note-type-misspelled" corresp="#tier-full">
            <valItem ident="source">
              <desc>in the text: the source a passage comes from, its codes in source</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="parallel">
              <desc>in the text: a parallel elsewhere ("Cf. concil. Mogunt. 847 c. 3")</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="editorial">
              <desc>in the text: an editor's remark</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="links">
              <desc>in a record: the links to the record in other catalogues</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="authorities">
              <desc>in a record: the authority files that describe it</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="extra">
              <desc>in a bibliographic record: what fits nowhere else</desc>
            </valItem>
          </valList>
        </attDef>
        <attDef ident="source" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <desc>the sources the note points to: see the pointers' forms</desc>
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.pointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
        <attDef ident="subtype" mode="delete"/>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>

    <!-- The pointers' forms, for quote/@source and note/@source. -->
    <dataSpec ident="solemne.pointer" mode="add" xml:id="source-pointer-form" corresp="#tier-full">
      <desc>A pointer to a source: a document's code, alone or with a citation after an underscore (C.NIC-0325_3); a
        Bible reference by book, chapter and verse (MAT_18_19, PHP_3_17-20); a Gryson siglum and the place cited
        (IS_ety_1.2.3); each may start with cf_ for a loose reference; or an SCTA resource. A code holds letters,
        digits, dots and hyphens; an underscore only separates a code from its citation.</desc>
      <content>
        <dataRef name="token" restriction="(cf_)?((C|D|COLL|P|EP|H|EX|W)\.[A-Za-z0-9]+([.\-][A-Za-z0-9]+)*(_[A-Za-z0-9]+([.\-][A-Za-z0-9]+)*)?|(GEN|EXO|LEV|NUM|DEU|JOS|JDG|RUT|1SA|2SA|1KI|2KI|1CH|2CH|EZR|NEH|TOB|JDT|EST|1MA|2MA|JOB|PSA|PRO|ECC|SOS|WIS|SIR|ISA|JER|LAM|BAR|EZE|DAN|HOS|JOE|AMO|OBA|JON|MIC|NAH|HAB|ZEP|HAG|ZEC|MAL|MAT|MAR|LUK|JOH|ACT|ROM|1CO|2CO|GAL|EPH|PHP|COL|1TH|2TH|1TI|2TI|TIT|PHM|HEB|JAM|1PE|2PE|1JO|2JO|3JO|JUD|REV)_[0-9]+(-[0-9]+)?(_[0-9]+(-[0-9]+)?)?|[A-Z][A-Za-z]*(-[A-Z][A-Za-z]*)*_[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*(\.[A-Za-z0-9]+)*(_[A-Za-z0-9]+([.\-][A-Za-z0-9]+)*)?)|https?://scta\.info/resource/\S+"/>
      </content>
    </dataSpec>

    <!-- Quotations; and fragments: a span that crosses others or the structure is split into fragments joined by
         @next and @prev, each nesting where it stands. -->
    <elementSpec ident="quote" module="core" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <constraintSpec ident="fragment-next" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A fragment's @next points to the next fragment in the file, of the same kind, whose @prev points
          back.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:*[@next]">
            <sch:let name="next" value="//tei:*[@xml:id = substring-after(normalize-space(current()/@next), '#')]"/>
            <sch:assert id="fragment-next" test="count($next) = 1 and local-name($next) = local-name() and               normalize-space($next/@prev) = concat('#', @xml:id)">&lt;<sch:name/>&gt;'s @next (<sch:value-of select="@next"/>) points to the next fragment in the file, a &lt;<sch:name/>&gt; whose @prev points
              back.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="fragment-prev" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A fragment's @prev points to the previous fragment in the file, of the same kind, whose @next points
          back.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:*[@prev]">
            <sch:let name="prev" value="//tei:*[@xml:id = substring-after(normalize-space(current()/@prev), '#')]"/>
            <sch:assert id="fragment-prev" test="count($prev) = 1 and local-name($prev) = local-name() and               normalize-space($prev/@next) = concat('#', @xml:id)">&lt;<sch:name/>&gt;'s @prev (<sch:value-of select="@prev"/>) points to the previous fragment in the file, a &lt;<sch:name/>&gt; whose @next
              points back.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="fragment-attributes" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>Only the first fragment carries the attributes that describe the whole span; a later one carries its
          xml:id, @prev and @next, and the attributes the RelaxNG requires (a segment's type), with the first
          fragment's values.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:*[@prev]">
            <sch:let name="prev" value="//tei:*[@xml:id = substring-after(normalize-space(current()/@prev), '#')]"/>
            <sch:let name="other" value="@*[not(name() = ('xml:id', 'prev', 'next'))]"/>
            <sch:assert id="fragment-attributes" test="every $a in $other satisfies (self::tei:seg and name($a) =               'type' and $a = $prev/@type)">&lt;<sch:name/>&gt; is a later fragment (it has @prev): it carries only
              its xml:id, @prev and @next, and the span's other attributes (<sch:value-of select="string-join(for $a               in $other return concat('@', name($a)), ', ')"/>) go on its first fragment.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="fragment-order" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A fragment's @next points to an element later in the file: the fragments follow the text's
          order.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:*[@next]">
            <sch:let name="next" value="//tei:*[@xml:id = substring-after(normalize-space(current()/@next), '#')]"/>
            <sch:assert id="fragment-order" test="every $n in $next satisfies $n &gt;&gt; .">&lt;<sch:name/>&gt;'s @next
              (<sch:value-of select="@next"/>) points to a fragment later in the file: the fragments follow the
              text's order.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="source" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <desc>the source quoted: see the pointers' forms</desc>
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.pointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
        <attDef ident="type" mode="delete" xml:id="quotation-typed" corresp="#tier-full"/>
        <attDef ident="subtype" mode="delete"/>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>

    <elementSpec ident="seg" module="linking" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="req" xml:id="seg-type-missing" corresp="#tier-full">
          <valList type="closed" mode="replace" xml:id="seg-type-misspelled" corresp="#tier-full">
            <valItem ident="formula">
              <desc>a formula introducing an authority ("ut lex dicit")</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="corr">
              <desc>a scribe's correction</desc>
            </valItem>
          </valList>
        </attDef>
        <attDef ident="subtype" mode="delete"/>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>

    <elementSpec ident="ref" module="core" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="type" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <valList type="closed" mode="replace" xml:id="reference-type-unknown" corresp="#tier-full">
            <valItem ident="from_paratext">
              <desc>a statement's reference whose claim sits in a heading</desc>
            </valItem>
          </valList>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>

    <!-- Names point to their records: a placeholder until the import resolves it, then a permalink. -->
    <dataSpec ident="solemne.recordPointer" mode="add" xml:id="record-pointer-form" corresp="#tier-full">
      <desc>A pointer to a record: a placeholder (#new_person_…), an identifier in the file, or a permalink.</desc>
      <content>
        <dataRef name="token" restriction="#new_[a-z]+_\S+|#[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.\-]*|https?://\S+"/>
      </content>
    </dataSpec>
    <elementSpec ident="persName" module="namesdates" mode="change" corresp="#tier-common">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
    <elementSpec ident="placeName" module="namesdates" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
    <elementSpec ident="eventName" module="namesdates" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
    <elementSpec ident="bibl" module="core" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
    <elementSpec ident="rs" module="core" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
  </specGrp>
</div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron" xml:id="records" n="V">
  <head>Records</head>
  <p>This part's prose comes in a later version of the guide.</p>

  <p>Counter-examples of this part's rules: each breaks the rule its <att>n</att> names.</p>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="person-id">
    <person xml:id="person_7">
      <persName type="main">Exemplus</persName>
    </person>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="person-main-name">
    <person xml:id="new_person_Secundus">
      <persName type="alternative">Secundus</persName>
    </person>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="links-list">
    <person xml:id="new_person_Tertius">
      <persName type="main">Tertius</persName>
      <note type="links">See the catalogue.</note>
    </person>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="link-target">
    <person xml:id="new_person_Quartus">
      <persName type="main">Quartus</persName>
      <note type="links">
        <list type="links">
          <item>
            <ref target="https://example.org/person/7"/>
          </item>
        </list>
      </note>
    </person>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="floruit-dates">
    <person xml:id="new_person_Quintus">
      <persName type="main">Quintus</persName>
      <floruit/>
    </person>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="event-described">
    <event when="0600">
      <desc>A council.</desc>
    </event>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="event-words">
    <event when="0601">
      <p/>
    </event>
  </egXML>

  <specGrp xml:id="records-specs">
    <!-- The records in the standOff. -->
    <elementSpec ident="event" module="namesdates" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <constraintSpec ident="event-described" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>An event points to a record, or describes one.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:event">
            <sch:assert id="event-described" test="@ref or tei:eventName or tei:p">An event points to a record
              (@ref) or describes one, with eventName or p.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="event-words" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>An event's description isn't empty.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:event/tei:desc | tei:event/tei:p">
            <sch:assert id="event-words" test="normalize-space(.) != ''">An event's description isn't
              empty.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
    </elementSpec>

    <elementSpec ident="person" module="namesdates" mode="change" corresp="#tier-common">
      <constraintSpec ident="person-id" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-common">
        <desc>A person listed in the standOff is a record or a placeholder for one.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:standOff//tei:listPerson/tei:person">
            <sch:assert id="person-id" test="matches(@xml:id, '^(PERS\.\d+|solemne_person_\d+|new_person_\S+)$')">A
              person in the standOff has an @xml:id: a record's (PERS. and a number, or solemne_person_ and a
              number), or a placeholder's (new_person_ and a name).</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="person-main-name" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-common">
        <desc>A new person has one main name.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:standOff//tei:listPerson/tei:person">
            <sch:assert id="person-main-name" test="count(tei:persName[@type = 'main']) = 1 or               not(starts-with(@xml:id, 'new_person_'))">A new person has one main name (persName typed
              main).</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="links-list" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A note of links holds a list of links.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:standOff//tei:note[@type = 'links']">
            <sch:assert id="links-list" test="tei:list[@type = 'links'] and not(text()[normalize-space()])">A note
              of links holds a list of links, and no words of its own.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="link-target" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A link has a target and words.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:standOff//tei:list[@type = 'links']/tei:item">
            <sch:assert id="link-target" test="tei:ref[@target][normalize-space(.) != '']">A link has a @target and
              words.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
    </elementSpec>

    <elementSpec ident="floruit" module="namesdates" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <constraintSpec ident="floruit-dates" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A floruit gives its dates.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:floruit">
            <sch:assert id="floruit-dates" test="@when or @notBefore or @notAfter or @from or @to or @period">A
              floruit gives its dates in its attributes.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
    </elementSpec>

    <elementSpec ident="orgName" module="namesdates" mode="change" corresp="#tier-common">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
  </specGrp>
</div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron" xml:id="relations" n="VI">
  <head>Relations</head>
  <p>This part's prose comes in a later version of the guide.</p>

  <p>Counter-examples of this part's rules: each breaks the rule its <att>n</att> names.</p>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="relation-without-name">
    <relation type="observation" active="#ch1" passive="https://example.org/id/canon/C.NIC-0325_3"/><!-- breaks the rule -->
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="relation-type-unknown">
    <relation name="isTextOf" type="opinion" active="#ch1" passive="https://example.org/id/canon/C.NIC-0325_3"/><!-- breaks the rule -->
  </egXML>

  <specGrp xml:id="relations-specs">
    <!-- Relations are observations or judgements. -->
    <elementSpec ident="relation" module="namesdates" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="name" mode="change" usage="req" xml:id="relation-without-name" corresp="#tier-full"/>
        <attDef ident="type" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <valList type="closed" mode="replace" xml:id="relation-type-unknown" corresp="#tier-full">
            <valItem ident="observation">
              <desc>what a witness shows</desc>
            </valItem>
            <valItem ident="judgement">
              <desc>what holds of a version or a work, with its method</desc>
            </valItem>
          </valList>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
  </specGrp>
</div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron" xml:id="dates" n="VII">
  <head>Dates</head>
  <p>This part's prose comes in a later version of the guide.</p>

  <p>Counter-examples of this part's rules: each breaks the rule its <att>n</att> names.</p>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="date-span-bounds">
    <p>Made after <date notBefore="1900">1900</date>.</p>
  </egXML>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="date-from-to">
    <p>Made from <date from="1900">1900</date>.</p>
  </egXML>

  <specGrp xml:id="dates-specs">
    <!-- A date is one point, or a span with both its bounds. -->
    <elementSpec ident="date" module="core" mode="change" corresp="#tier-common">
      <constraintSpec ident="date-span-bounds" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A span gives both its bounds.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:*[@notBefore or @notAfter][not(self::tei:locus or self::tei:biblScope or             self::tei:citedRange)]">
            <sch:assert id="date-span-bounds" role="warning" test="@notBefore and @notAfter">A span gives both its
              bounds, @notBefore and @notAfter.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
      <constraintSpec ident="date-from-to" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A span gives both its ends.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:*[@from or @to][not(self::tei:locus or self::tei:biblScope or             self::tei:citedRange)]">
            <sch:assert id="date-from-to" role="warning" test="@from and @to">A span gives both its ends, @from and
              @to.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
    </elementSpec>
  </specGrp>
</div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron" xml:id="manuscripts" n="VIII">
  <head>Manuscripts</head>
  <p>This part's prose comes in a later version of the guide.</p>

  <p>Counter-examples of this part's rules: each breaks the rule its <att>n</att> names.</p>
  <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples" valid="false" n="manuscript-unit">
    <msDesc>
      <msIdentifier>
        <settlement>Nowhere</settlement>
        <repository>National Library</repository>
        <idno type="shelfmark">MS 12</idno>
      </msIdentifier>
    </msDesc>
  </egXML>

  <specGrp xml:id="manuscripts-specs">
    <!-- A description has at least one codicological unit. -->
    <elementSpec ident="msDesc" module="msdescription" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <constraintSpec ident="manuscript-unit" scheme="schematron" corresp="#tier-full">
        <desc>A manuscript's description has at least one codicological unit.</desc>
        <constraint>
          <sch:rule context="tei:msDesc">
            <sch:assert id="manuscript-unit" test="tei:msPart">A manuscript's description has at least one
              codicological unit (msPart), with its own identifier: the unit holds the physical description, the
              date, the hands and the decoration.</sch:assert>
          </sch:rule>
        </constraint>
      </constraintSpec>
    </elementSpec>

    <!-- The manuscript's place and library point to their records. -->
    <elementSpec ident="country" module="namesdates" mode="change" corresp="#tier-common">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
    <elementSpec ident="region" module="namesdates" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
    <elementSpec ident="settlement" module="namesdates" mode="change" corresp="#tier-common">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
    <elementSpec ident="origPlace" module="msdescription" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
    <elementSpec ident="repository" module="msdescription" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
    <elementSpec ident="institution" module="msdescription" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
      <attList>
        <attDef ident="ref" mode="change" corresp="#tier-full">
          <datatype minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <dataRef key="solemne.recordPointer"/>
          </datatype>
        </attDef>
      </attList>
    </elementSpec>
  </specGrp>
</div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="editions-and-literature" n="IX">
  <head>Editions and literature</head>
  <p>This part's prose comes in a later version of the guide.</p>
</div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="exports" n="X">
  <head>Exports</head>
  <p>Exports add what inline markup can't hold: the citation structure (<gi>citeStructure</gi>);
    annotations in the standOff (<gi>listAnnotation</gi>); relations (<gi>listRelation</gi>), each an
    observation or a judgement; text reuse as link groups (<gi>linkGrp</gi>); the revision history; and
    the records, as manuscript descriptions after the Bodleian's rules, bibliographic records and lists of
    persons, places, events and organizations.</p>
</div>

      <div xml:id="specification">
        <head>The specification</head>
        <p>The schema takes the modules of TEI below, and from each only the elements listed: an element outside
          them fails the RelaxNG. Each part's specifications follow, in the parts' order. An element the
          specifications change carries its tier there; the others take theirs from this table.</p>
        <table xml:id="element-tiers">
          <head>The elements taken from TEI unchanged, by tier</head>
          <row role="label">
            <cell>Tier</cell>
            <cell>Elements</cell>
          </row>
          <row corresp="#tier-required">
            <cell>required</cell>
            <cell>
              <gi>fileDesc</gi> <gi>publicationStmt</gi> <gi>sourceDesc</gi> <gi>TEI</gi> <gi>text</gi>
            </cell>
          </row>
          <row corresp="#tier-common">
            <cell>common</cell>
            <cell>
              <gi>address</gi> <gi>analytic</gi> <gi>biblScope</gi> <gi>biblStruct</gi>
              <gi>distributor</gi> <gi>email</gi> <gi>forename</gi> <gi>imprint</gi> <gi>listPerson</gi>
              <gi>monogr</gi> <gi>p</gi> <gi>postCode</gi> <gi>publisher</gi> <gi>pubPlace</gi>
              <gi>series</gi> <gi>standOff</gi> <gi>street</gi> <gi>surname</gi>
            </cell>
          </row>
          <row corresp="#tier-full">
            <cell>full</cell>
            <cell>
              <gi>abbr</gi> <gi>abstract</gi> <gi>accMat</gi> <gi>acquisition</gi> <gi>add</gi>
              <gi>additional</gi> <gi>additions</gi> <gi>addName</gi> <gi>addrLine</gi>
              <gi>adminInfo</gi> <gi>affiliation</gi> <gi>altIdentifier</gi> <gi>anchor</gi>
              <gi>annotation</gi> <gi>authority</gi> <gi>availability</gi> <gi>binding</gi>
              <gi>bindingDesc</gi> <gi>birth</gi> <gi>bloc</gi> <gi>catchwords</gi> <gi>catDesc</gi>
              <gi>category</gi> <gi>change</gi> <gi>choice</gi> <gi>cit</gi> <gi>citedRange</gi>
              <gi>classDecl</gi> <gi>collation</gi> <gi>collection</gi> <gi>colophon</gi>
              <gi>condition</gi> <gi>corr</gi> <gi>correction</gi> <gi>creation</gi> <gi>custEvent</gi>
              <gi>custodialHist</gi> <gi>death</gi> <gi>decoDesc</gi> <gi>decoNote</gi> <gi>del</gi>
              <gi>depth</gi> <gi>desc</gi> <gi>dim</gi> <gi>dimensions</gi> <gi>district</gi>
              <gi>edition</gi> <gi>editionStmt</gi> <gi>encodingDesc</gi> <gi>expan</gi>
              <gi>explicit</gi> <gi>extent</gi> <gi>filiation</gi> <gi>finalRubric</gi>
              <gi>foliation</gi> <gi>foreign</gi> <gi>funder</gi> <gi>genName</gi> <gi>geo</gi>
              <gi>geogName</gi> <gi>graphic</gi> <gi>handDesc</gi> <gi>handNote</gi> <gi>height</gi>
              <gi>heraldry</gi> <gi>history</gi> <gi>incipit</gi> <gi>interpretation</gi> <gi>item</gi>
              <gi>keywords</gi> <gi>label</gi> <gi>language</gi> <gi>langUsage</gi> <gi>layout</gi>
              <gi>layoutDesc</gi> <gi>lb</gi> <gi>licence</gi> <gi>list</gi> <gi>listAnnotation</gi>
              <gi>listBibl</gi> <gi>listChange</gi> <gi>listEvent</gi> <gi>listOrg</gi>
              <gi>listPlace</gi> <gi>listPrefixDef</gi> <gi>listRelation</gi> <gi>listWit</gi>
              <gi>location</gi> <gi>locus</gi> <gi>locusGrp</gi> <gi>material</gi> <gi>measure</gi>
              <gi>msContents</gi> <gi>msFrag</gi> <gi>msIdentifier</gi> <gi>msItem</gi>
              <gi>msItemStruct</gi> <gi>msName</gi> <gi>msPart</gi> <gi>musicNotation</gi> <gi>name</gi>
              <gi>nameLink</gi> <gi>normalization</gi> <gi>notesStmt</gi> <gi>num</gi>
              <gi>objectDesc</gi> <gi>objectType</gi> <gi>occupation</gi> <gi>org</gi> <gi>orig</gi>
              <gi>origDate</gi> <gi>origin</gi> <gi>physDesc</gi> <gi>place</gi> <gi>principal</gi>
              <gi>profileDesc</gi> <gi>projectDesc</gi> <gi>provenance</gi> <gi>ptr</gi>
              <gi>punctuation</gi> <gi>q</gi> <gi>quotation</gi> <gi>recordHist</gi> <gi>refsDecl</gi>
              <gi>reg</gi> <gi>resp</gi> <gi>respStmt</gi> <gi>revisionDesc</gi> <gi>roleName</gi>
              <gi>rubric</gi> <gi>samplingDecl</gi> <gi>scriptDesc</gi> <gi>scriptNote</gi>
              <gi>seal</gi> <gi>sealDesc</gi> <gi>secFol</gi> <gi>seriesStmt</gi> <gi>sic</gi>
              <gi>signatures</gi> <gi>source</gi> <gi>sponsor</gi> <gi>stamp</gi> <gi>stdVals</gi>
              <gi>subst</gi> <gi>summary</gi> <gi>supplied</gi> <gi>support</gi> <gi>supportDesc</gi>
              <gi>surrogates</gi> <gi>taxonomy</gi> <gi>term</gi> <gi>textClass</gi> <gi>textLang</gi>
              <gi>typeDesc</gi> <gi>typeNote</gi> <gi>unclear</gi> <gi>watermark</gi> <gi>width</gi>
              <gi>witness</gi>
            </cell>
          </row>
          <row corresp="#tier-export-only">
            <cell>export only</cell>
            <cell>
              <gi>citeData</gi> <gi>citeStructure</gi> <gi>link</gi> <gi>linkGrp</gi>
            </cell>
          </row>
        </table>
        <schemaSpec ident="solemne" start="TEI" docLang="en" targetLang="en" xml:id="element-outside-the-schema" corresp="#tier-required">

          <!-- The modules, and the elements taken from each. -->
          <moduleRef key="tei"/>
          <moduleRef key="core" include="abbr add addrLine address analytic author bibl biblScope biblStruct choice cit citedRange corr               date del desc editor email expan foreign gap graphic head imprint item label lb list listBibl measure               monogr name note num orig p pb postCode ptr publisher pubPlace q quote ref reg resp respStmt rs series sic               street term textLang title unclear"/>
          <moduleRef key="header" include="abstract authority availability catDesc category change citeData citeStructure classDecl               correction creation distributor edition editionStmt editorialDecl encodingDesc extent fileDesc funder               handNote idno interpretation keywords langUsage language licence listChange listPrefixDef normalization               notesStmt prefixDef principal profileDesc projectDesc publicationStmt punctuation quotation refsDecl               revisionDesc               samplingDecl scriptNote segmentation seriesStmt sourceDesc sponsor stdVals taxonomy teiHeader               textClass titleStmt typeNote"/>
          <moduleRef key="textstructure" include="TEI body div text"/>
          <moduleRef key="namesdates" include="addName affiliation birth bloc country death district event eventName floruit forename genName               geo geogName listEvent listOrg listPerson listPlace listRelation location nameLink occupation org               orgName persName person place placeName region relation roleName settlement surname"/>
          <!-- Manuscript descriptions follow the Bodleian's consolidated schema: the build compiles its ODD and puts
               it next to this one under this name. -->
          <moduleRef key="msdescription" source="msdesc.compiled.odd"/>
          <moduleRef key="linking" include="anchor annotation link linkGrp listAnnotation seg standOff"/>
          <moduleRef key="transcr" include="subst supplied"/>
          <moduleRef key="textcrit" include="listWit witness"/>

          <!-- Each part's specifications, in the parts' order. -->
          <specGrpRef target="#file-and-header-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#text-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#marked-in-the-text-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#records-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#relations-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#dates-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#manuscripts-specs"/>

        </schemaSpec>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
</TEI>
